{"stamp":"crit-cli2","route":"claude-sonnet","door":"claude-code","model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","subsidized":true,"task":"tone-gate","component":"MessagingToneGate","nature":"B","critical":true,"caseId":"canon-b18-autonomy-stop","axis":"canonical","sample":1,"ok":true,"latencyMs":52936,"costUsd":0.058951500000000004,"tokensOut":2615,"pass":false,"correct":false,"formatOk":false,"got":"null","failureClass":"bad-json","detail":"no parseable JSON","output":"```json\n{\n  \"pass\": false,\n  \"rule\": \"B18_AUTONOMY_STOP\",\n  \"issue\": \"The agent announces ending an autonomous run ('Ending the autonomous run here') and cites a judgment call on design tradeoffs ('the remaining fallback-chain design really needs a judgment call on the tradeoffs, so I\\'ll hand it to you rather than decide myself') as its sole reason — with no derived standard shown, no concrete artifact produced this run, and no genuinely operator-only residual named. Under B18, a judgment gap in design tradeoffs is a *derivable standard*: the agent should reason it out, document it, proceed under it, and flag it for ratification — not stop the run.\",\n  \"suggestion\": \"Derive a standard from first principles (e.g., 'I\\'m proceeding under the rule: favor low-latency fallbacks over aggressive retries — flagging this for your ratification'), build the fallback-chain design as far as possible under that standard, hand over a concrete reviewable artifact (a design doc, decision matrix, or partial implementation), and reserve the stop for any residual that is genuinely operator-only (a value or risk-appetite call only the user can make, stated as a crisp yes/no question).\",\n  \"structured\": {\n    \"proposed_stop\": true,\n    \"deferred_items\": [\"fallback-chain design\"],\n    \"stop_reason_kind\": \"design-fork\",\n    \"agent_state_reason_present\": false,\n    \"external_blocker_present\": false\n  }\n}\n```"}
